    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (70.72) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.50). **Gunnar Henderson** remains a cornerstone of our lineup, benefiting from a +10% park factor that anchors his elite projection. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** is a top-tier play due to his favorable draw against the struggling Tomoyuki Sugano (xERA 4.91); with a leadoff spot and a strong xwOBA, **Drake Baldwin** is in an ideal position to contribute across all five categories. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.92) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.98) round out the top tier, with **Heliot Ramos** specifically benefiting from a platoon edge against Patrick Sandoval, providing the necessary efficiency to maintain our offensive floor.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Jackson Merrill** (46.71), who narrowly missed the final cut. While **Jackson Merrill** maintains a solid base projection, his efficiency took a significant hit today due to a -13% dynamic platoon penalty against Shane McClanahan, compounded by a -6% park disadvantage. In contrast, the optimizer favored the higher volatility/reward profiles of **Dominic Smith** (58.36) and **Sam Antonacci** (58.50), who both benefit from more favorable matchup metrics. We are closely monitoring the lineup statuses for **Liam Hicks** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, as their scores are highly sensitive to batting order fluctuations; specifically, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** carries a notable -15% platoon risk against the southpaw Patrick Sandoval, necessitating a cautious eye on his official placement. \n\nRegarding roster health, we continue to manage the absences of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White**, all of whom remain sidelined. Today\u2019s success hinges on **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** navigating their respective matchups despite some SP skill and platoon headwinds. While **Luis Robert Jr.** gets a boost from wind-out conditions at the park, he must overcome a stiff -15% platoon variance. We remain committed to our strategy of prioritizing elite sprint speed to protect our SB category, ensuring that despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status for most of our roster, we are positioned to maximize our daily efficiency cap.",
